h3 2.7 Safe passing of structured data
text "To support passing JavaScript objects, including , across  boundaries, this specification defines the following infrastructure for serializing and deserializing objects, including in some cases transferring the underlying data instead of copying it. Collectively this serialization/deserialization process is known as \"structured cloning\", although most APIs perform separate serialization and deserialization steps. (With the notable exception being the  method.)"
link "platform objects" https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object
link realm https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms
link structuredClone() #dom-structuredclone
text This section uses the terminology and typographic conventions from the JavaScript specification.
link [JAVASCRIPT] references.html#refsJAVASCRIPT
